7. ExplOri 22.5 — Brandon Wong (theplantpsychologist)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Service, not a port. Nothing from ExplOri is vendored, ported, or bundled, so
this section carries no license grant to reproduce — it is here because the
Search 22.5° design method does not work without someone else's server, and a
reader of this file should know that.

Upstream service: https://225.designorigami.net (built on
             https://github.com/theplantpsychologist/SEARCH-22.5)
Consumed by: apps/web/src/explori/ (client) and
             apps/web/functions/api/explori/ + functions/_lib/explori.ts (the
             Cloudflare Pages Function that proxies it; the browser cannot call
             upstream directly, since it sends no CORS headers)

  The Search 22.5° design kind sends a user's drawn tree to that service and
  displays the crease patterns it returns from a precomputed archive of 22.5°
  tilings. There is no optimizer and no local archive: every result is upstream
  data, fetched per query and not redistributed by us.

  Permission to build the integration was given by theplantpsychologist; see
  implementation-plans/explori-design-type.md. The service's own terms are not
  published, and the archive contents carry no stated license — so results are
  treated as the service's to give, and the only copy of any of it in this
  repository is the single captured response used as a test fixture
  (apps/web/src/explori/__fixtures__/queryResponse.json).

  Upstream logs the query tree, the caller's IP, and request headers. The app
  tells users their tree leaves the machine; that notice is a feature notice and
  is deliberately not gated on the analytics opt-out.
